  "description": "FUZBEL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H96 Co2 Eu4 N6 O36. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 9 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.286-4.051 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.16-114.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C48H96Co2Eu4N6O36. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
